94
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:22,600
structural advantages over actual scheming
models for control evaluations.

95
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:26,790
To provide meaningful safety guarantees,
red teams must elicit

96
00:06:26,790 --> 00:06:30,829
capabilities comparable to what highly
capable scheming models might

97
00:06:30,829 --> 00:06:34,509
deploy in the wild. This might seem
impossible since

98
00:06:34,509 --> 00:06:37,709
we're evaluating AI systems that could be
smarter than

99
00:06:37,709 --> 00:06:40,670
humans. In some ways, the Red team in
control

100
00:06:40,670 --> 00:06:44,430
evaluations have some advantages to ensure
we can appropriately

101
00:06:44,430 --> 00:06:47,829
simulate this scenario. 1. The red team
can spend

102
00:06:47,829 --> 00:06:51,240
much more time analyzing potential attacks
than the AI

103
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:54,560
would have during deployment. While an AI
might need

104
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:57,639
to make decisions in a single forward
pass, the

105
00:06:57,639 --> 00:07:00,319
red team can iterate on strategies over
weeks or

106
00:07:00,319 --> 00:07:04,759
months. 2. The Red Team has complete
information about

107
00:07:04,759 --> 00:07:07,680
the safety measures being used so they can
come

108
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:11,680
up with potentially more advanced
strategies. 3. The Red

109
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:14,160
Team can learn from failed attempts and
iterate on

110
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:17,439
their methods, while an AI system caught
