review.

136
00:09:04,730 --> 00:09:09,990
5. Software infrastructure comprehensive
logging systems Fine grained permission

137
00:09:09,990 --> 00:09:13,750
management, artifact tracking and
scaffolding that supports blocking or

138
00:09:13,750 --> 00:09:17,909
resampling suspicious outputs create an
environment where AI actions

139
00:09:17,909 --> 00:09:23,789
are consistently monitored. 6. Adversarial
evaluation and training Continuous

140
00:09:23,789 --> 00:09:27,710
red teaming tests all safety components
against realistic attack

141
00:09:27,710 --> 00:09:32,190
scenarios using synthetic data generation
to create plausible but

142
00:09:32,190 --> 00:09:37,440
challenging inputs that probe for
weaknesses. 7. Security Enhancements

143
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:42,000
Hardware enforced code signing, bandwidth
limitations within data centers

144
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:46,879
and multilevel shutdown mechanisms provide
critical infrastructure protection against

145
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:51,279
unauthorized operations. For example, when
testing whether an AI

146
00:09:51,279 --> 00:09:54,919
agent can exfiltrate sensitive data, the
blue team might

147
00:09:54,919 --> 00:09:58,639
implement not just content filters but
also bandwidth monitoring,

148
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:03,870
permission restrictions and random human
audits creating multiple independent

149
00:10:03,870 --> 00:10:07,710
failure points. The Red team must
simultaneously overcome control

150
00:10:07,710 --> 00:10:12,110
evaluations, prioritize defense against
the most severe threat categories.

151
00:10:12,669 --> 00:10:16,070
When designing control measures, not all
potential threats pose

152
00:10:16,070 --> 00:10:20,750
equal risk. Rogue internal deployments
represent the highest priority

153
00:10:20,750 --> 00:10:25,029
threat where AI systems gain unmonitored
compute access and

154
00:10:25,029 --> 00:10:30,039
potentially elevated permissions. Within
developer infrastructure, this ranks above

155
00:10:30,039 --> 00:10:33,799
sabotage of safety critical work, which
itself ranks above

156
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:38,519
other security failures, including self
exfiltration where AI models

157
00:10:38,519 --> 00:10:43,200
steal their own weights. This
prioritization framework helps allocate

158
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:47,399
limited security resources toward
preventing the most consequential failure

159
00:10:47,399 --> 00:10:52,759
modes first, particularly when constraints
prevent implementing comprehensive
protections

160
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:56,740
against all possible threats. For more
information on details

161
00:10:56,740 --> 00:11:01,059
of different subcategories of control
evaluations and prioritization between

162
00:11:01,059 --> 00:11:06,100
them, please read the Appendix. Eliciting
